SUMMARY:Palm Sunday litany of Agios Spyridon\, Corfu town
LOCATION:Corfu town\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The longest of the litanies\, commemorating the 1630 plague\, takes the saint's body right around the old town on Palm Sunday morning with all eighteen or so philharmonic bands of the island playing\; it is the start of Corfu's famous Easter week\, which continues with the Holy Saturday litany and the pot-throwing. Come at 11am and stand near the Spianada to hear the bands cross.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#corfu-town-palm-sunday-litany-of-agios-spyridon-corfu-town
